    <string name="onboarding_welcome_title">Welcome to DailyBeat</string>
    <string name="onboarding_welcome_body">Remember where your day took you, add notes and review a journal on your phone. No account or AI is needed. Online maps contact map providers. Automatic place lookup is off until you configure it. Cloud AI and cloud backup are optional and have separate privacy choices.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_officer_title">Make it your journal</string>
    <string name="onboarding_officer_body">Choose a template. Your optional name appears on exports. You can change both in Settings.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_privacy_title">Capture is your choice</string>
    <string name="onboarding_privacy_body">Location — allow background location if you want your route recorded while the phone is in your pocket. Approximate location works with less detail. You can also use notes and diaries without location.\n\nNotifications — show capture status and a review reminder. On supported builds, motion permission helps reduce location work while stationary.\n\nPause or switch capture off in Settings at any time. Private zones limit outgoing records; always review free-text notes before sharing.\n\nOnline maps are on by default and contact map providers. Turn them off in Capture &amp; Places. Tamil Nadu downloads are a separate internet action and provide offline street maps. Address lookup stays off unless you configure and enable it.</string>
